{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"Rule 6c-11 does **not** make every authorized participant a signatory to the AP agreement. It permits an ETF to transact in creation units with an AP that is a registered clearing agency member or has a clearing-agency-member agreement with one; the AP must also be a broker-dealer or other eligible institution.\n\nIn the reviewed **U.S. forms**, the main contract is typically between the **trust (for the relevant series)** and the **AP**. The trust is an existing legal entity, usually a registered investment company; the rule’s permitted-AP categories describe who may participate, not additional parties automatically bound by the form.\n\nThe **Irish ICAV** arrangement differs: the ICAV is the corporate fund vehicle, and the agreement commonly names the ICAV (or its management company) and AP, with custody/settlement roles addressed separately. The exact parties and status depend on each form; Rule 6c-11 itself does not determine them."}}
